{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788484706189,"sessionID":"ses_f9602b4c8ffeg2NhL92h7AtLNR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_e1c563c03ea14671aa4923fd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/aiogram/aiogram/pulls/1670 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['title']); print(d['body'][:500])\"; curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aiogram/aiogram/master/CHANGES/1670.bugfix.rst"},"output":"Add semaphore support for limiting concurrent updates\n# Description\r\n\r\nIntroduce a semaphore-based mechanism to control the number of concurrent tasks in polling mode when `handle_as_tasks=True`. Added the `tasks_concurrency_limit` parameter to `start_polling()` and `run_polling()`, preventing potential memory exhaustion during high update loads.\r\n\r\nFixes #1658\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n\r\n# Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [x] My code follows the style guidelines of this project\r\n- [x] I have performed a self-\n404: Not Found","metadata":{"output":"Add semaphore support for limiting concurrent updates\n# Description\r\n\r\nIntroduce a semaphore-based mechanism to control the number of concurrent tasks in polling mode when `handle_as_tasks=True`. Added the `tasks_concurrency_limit` parameter to `start_polling()` and `run_polling()`, preventing potential memory exhaustion during high update loads.\r\n\r\nFixes #1658\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n\r\n# Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [x] My code follows the style guidelines of this project\r\n- [x] I have performed a self-\n404: Not Found","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/aiogram/aiogram/pulls/1670 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d['title']); print(d['body'][:500])\"; curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aiogram/aiogram/master/CHANGES/1670.bugfix.rst","time