{"type":"text","timestamp":1788484854803,"sessionID":"ses_f9602b4c8ffeg2NhL92h7AtLNR","part":{"id":"prt_06a0103af001raTRgJXDVyS7YD","messageID":"msg_06a00e6e2001d1bozkudD1wtIG","sessionID":"ses_f9602b4c8ffeg2NhL92h7AtLNR","type":"text","text":"All done. The mypy errors are pre-existing in unrelated modules (flags.py, command.py, handler.py) — none in the changed files.\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n**`aiogram/dispatcher/dispatcher.py`**\n- Added `_process_with_semaphore()` (aiogram/dispatcher/dispatcher.py:324) — awaits the update processing coroutine and releases the semaphore in a `finally` block, so slots are freed on both success and failure.\n- `_polling()` (aiogram/dispatcher/dispatcher.py:338) now accepts `tasks_concurrency_limit: Optional[int] = None`. When `handle_as_tasks=True` and a limit is set, it creates an `asyncio.Semaphore`, acquires a slot before creating each task (new updates wait when the limit is reached), and releases it via the wrapper when the task finishes. With `None` (default) or `handle_as_tasks=False`, behavior is unchanged.\n- `start_polling()` (aiogram/dispatcher/dispatcher.py:514) and `run_polling()` (aiogram/dispatcher/dispatcher.py:616) accept the new parameter, documented in docstrings, and pass it through to `_polling()`.\n\n**`CHANGES/1658.bugfix.rst`** — changelog fragment documenting the memory-exhaustion fix and the new `tasks_concurrency_limit` parameter.\n\n**`tests/test_dispatcher/test_dispatcher.py`** — added tests covering: semaphore creation only for `handle_as_tasks=True` + limit set (parametrized), semaphore release on success and on exception, and end-to-end concurrency limiting (semaphore value restored after processing 5 updates with limit 2).\n\nAll 128 dispatcher tests pass.","time":{"start":1788484846511,"end":1788484854797}}}
